  log-linear attention and TTT-Linear layers or reference ops adapt its layers
  and naive implementations, and the context-parallel state passing follows
  its fla/ops/cp design. The gated RMSNorm backward of the fused Mamba-2
  output glue (src/jla/layers/mamba2_fused.py) follows
  fla/modules/fused_norm_gate.py. Forming the LM-head gradient in the forward
  pass (src/jla/ops/mosaic_gpu/linear_cross_entropy.py) follows the design of
  its FusedLinearCrossEntropyLoss (design only, no code copied). The
  "upstream" initialisation reimplements its init schemes:
  fla/models/mamba2/modeling_mamba2.py and fla/models/mamba3/modeling_mamba3.py
  (rescale_prenorm_residual), fla/models/modeling_utils.py (_init_weights:
  nn.Conv1d at normal(0, initializer_range)), fla/layers/rwkv7.py (zero
  o_proj), fla/layers/rwkv6.py (LoRA: zero down, orthogonal up with gain 0.1)
  and fla/models/rwkv7/modeling_rwkv7.py (zero channel-mix value).

