* FlashAttention (https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention)
  Copyright (c) 2022, the respective contributors, as shown by its AUTHORS
  file. BSD 3-Clause License (licenses/flash-attention.LICENSE).
  The attention forward's intra-warpgroup overlap, warp-scheduler turns and
  192 x 128 tiles for head dim 64 follow hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
  and hopper/tile_size.h (design only, no code copied).
  The attention forward's persistent tile loop, its longest-first tile order
  inside L2-sized sections of (batch, head) pairs, its packed-document tiles
  sorted by key-block count, and the next tile's query load issued once the
  current tile's last QK^T has read the query tile follow
  hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp, hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h and
  hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp (design only, no code copied;
  src/jla/ops/mosaic_gpu/attention_persistent.py).
  The attention backward's block ranges and warpgroup layout follow
  hopper/mainloop_bwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp and hopper/block.h (design only, no
  code copied), and so does the fused one-kernel backward
  (backward="fused" in src/jla/ops/mosaic_gpu/attention.py: dS staged in
  shared memory as the dQ operand, dQ split over the consumer warpgroups, fp32
  dQ added with TMA reductions and rounded afterwards; design only, no code
  copied). The attention backward's longest-first CTA order inside L2-sized
  sections of (batch, head) pairs and its 24-register TMA warpgroup follow
  hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp (SingleTileBwdLPTScheduler) and
  hopper/flash_bwd_kernel_sm90.h (24 / 240 registers; design only, no code
  copied; src/jla/ops/mosaic_gpu/attention.py and attention_fp8_bwd.py).
  FlashAttention-3 is the attention baseline in
  benchmarks/torch_fa3.py (run by benchmarks/bench_attention_fa3.py),
  benchmarks/torch_fa3_mla.py (MLA's 192/128 head
  dims; benchmarks/build_fa3_mla.sh builds it from source with those head
  dims, setting its build flags only) and benchmarks/attention_fa3_diff.py, and the flame
  baseline runs it through benchmarks/end_to_end/1p3b/flame/fa3_shim, which
  re-exports its names and contains none of its code.

