Gated DeltaNet-2 is implemented from the equations of "Gated DeltaNet-2:
Decoupling Erase and Write in Linear Attention" (Hatamizadeh, Choi and Kautz,
arXiv:2605.22791). No code from its reference implementation is included.

The mLSTM recurrence is implemented from the equations of "xLSTM: Extended Long
Short-Term Memory" (arXiv:2405.04517) and the xLSTM 7B paper (arXiv:2503.13427).
No code from NX-AI/mlstm_kernels is included: benchmarks/torch_mlstm.py and
benchmarks/torch_upstream_diff.py call its public API as an optional baseline
from a separate environment (its NXAI Community License is not a permissive
licence).

The following projects are named in the documentation or run only as
benchmark baselines from separate environments; no code from them is included
or adapted: PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), causal-conv1d (BSD-3-Clause), cuDNN
(through JAX and PyTorch), Triton (the language of the FLA, Mamba and TFLA
baselines), torchtitan (the trainer library under the flame baseline),
grouped_gemm (https://github.com/tgale96/grouped_gemm, the CUTLASS grouped GEMM
that MegaBlocks uses; an optional baseline of benchmarks/bench_ragged_dot.py) and
MegaBlocks, Megatron-Core, quack, ThunderKittens and TileLang (TileLang runs
the official Mamba-3 MIMO kernels in the Mamba-3 MIMO baseline). The kimi-linear-1p3b and qwen3-next-1p3b
presets copy hyperparameters (field values only, no code or weights) from the
config.json files of moonshotai/Kimi-Linear-48B-A3B-Instruct and
Qwen/Qwen3-Next-80B-A3B-Instruct on the Hugging Face Hub.

The optional extras install and call these packages through their public APIs
only (none of their code is included): lm-evaluation-harness (jla eval
lm-eval, src/jla/eval/lm_eval_adapter.py), Orbax, Hugging Face datasets,
PyArrow, jinja2, Weights & Biases and tensorboardX. The runtime dependencies
(JAX and jaxlib with XLA and the CUDA libraries they bring, such as cuDNN,
cuBLAS and cuBLASLt, CUB, NCCL and CUPTI; Optax; NumPy) are likewise used
through their public APIs and keep their own licences. runtime.cluster_env reads the environment variables
of the SLURM, Open MPI and torchrun launchers; the benchmarks record NVIDIA's
nvidia-smi output, and benchmarks/kda.md and benchmarks/attention.md name
Nsight (not used).

The end-to-end benchmarks train on FineWeb-Edu
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-edu, ODC-By 1.0)
tokenized with Meta's Llama 3 tokenizer (128,256 ids, as shipped with Llama 3.1
and 3.2 under their community licences). Neither the data nor the tokenizer
is included.
